/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  F28 -- THE ACTUATOR DISK.  A uniform axial momentum source on the cellZone
  `disk`.  NO BLADES, NO SWIRL, NO ROTATION.  "Actuator-disk representation; no
  rotor" (registration section 2.1).

  `volumeMode specific;` APPEARS HERE VERBATIM AND IS LOAD-BEARING.
  Registration section 2.4, from the v2606 source on this box
  (src/fvOptions/sources/general/semiImplicitSource/SemiImplicitSource.C):
    :534    volumeMode is READ WITH A `get`, not a defaulted lookup -- it is a
            REQUIRED entry.
    :537-540  `absolute` sets VDash_ = V_ (the CELL-ZONE VOLUME);
              `specific` leaves VDash_ = 1.
    :348,:357,:367  the supplied value is DIVIDED BY VDash_.
    :224    the class constructor's own default is vmAbsolute.
  So the same number means a TOTAL OVER THE ZONE under `absolute` and a
  PER-UNIT-VOLUME DENSITY under `specific`.  Under `absolute` this case would
  still mesh, still run, still converge to tight residuals, and produce a
  smooth, monotone, entirely wrong map.  `specific` is additionally
  WEDGE-INVARIANT: a per-unit-volume density is the same number at any wedge
  angle, whereas `absolute` would have to be rescaled by 5/360 and is one
  silent factor of 72 away from being wrong.

  THE VALUE IS AN ACCELERATION, NOT A FORCE DENSITY, AND THAT IS NOT THE
  DIRECTIVE'S ARITHMETIC.  Sanaa's CASE 2 section 2.3 writes
  `injectionRateSuSp = delta_p / t` in N/m^3.  That is correct for a
  COMPRESSIBLE solver.  `simpleFoam` is INCOMPRESSIBLE: its momentum equation
  is divided by rho and `constant/transportProperties` carries only nu, so the
  source the solver needs is

        Su_x = delta_p / (rho * t)   [m/s^2]
             = 1000 / (1.2 * 0.005)  = 166666.666666667

  The two readings differ by rho = 1.2 -- A FACTOR OF 1.2, which is exactly the
  size that reads as a modelling detail rather than an error.  Control C3
  (registration section 6.2) computes T_disk two independent ways and closes on
  it: arm (a) is analytic from delta_p, arm (b) integrates THIS number over the
  built cellZone and multiplies by WEDGE_SCALE = 72.
  REPORTED TO THE SUPERVISOR AS A DEPARTURE FROM THE DIRECTIVE'S UNITS.

  Sign, registration section 2.5: the source is +x -- it accelerates the fluid
  DOWNSTREAM.  Thrust is positive in -x and every reported force is the -x
  component times -1.

  delta_p for THIS file: 1000 Pa (the section 6.2 control loading and the
  section 9.3 / 9.4 / 9.6 gate loading).  Other loadings are written by
  `constant/fvOptions.template` through the launcher; NO DICTIONARY IS EVER
  HAND-EDITED.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile { version 2.0; format ascii; class dictionary; object fvOptions; }

actuatorDisk
{
    type            vectorSemiImplicitSource;
    selectionMode   cellZone;
    cellZone        disk;
    volumeMode      specific;
    sources
    {
        U           ((166666.666666667 0 0) 0);
    }
}
